From 98d072c8bd306e809cb6f937b539faef1d840a3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:49:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Inverse barometer on by default; JRA55 runs can start on any
 date
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

[atmosphere] inverse_barometer = true (default) passes #676's inverse_barometer option: GLORYS's η carries
no response to the atmospheric pressure that JRA55 applies to the model (issue #37), so the inverse-
barometer sea level is added to GLORYS's η at the open sides (Flather) and to the initial free surface.
Its domain mean is removed, so it moves no volume and leaves the volume control alone. false: as before.

jra55_read_fix.jl works around NumericalEarth's jra55_read_data, which splits the wrapped record indices
where the index equals 1, so that a JRA55 run starting on any day but 1 January fails while building the
river routing (MethodError: -(::Nothing, ::Int64)). Taken from fjp/nested; to be fixed upstream.

config_smoke_test_sep2005.toml: the smoke test from 1 to 5 September 2005, the validation year (Tsubouchi
et al. 2018), which exercises the JRA55 fix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
